[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/BlackBaground.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
Narrator: Catherine finds a tall, slender figure there, strangely handsome up close, gloved hands, a smirk that doesn't reach his eyes.
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/lake_side_nigh.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
audio music "res://assets/audio/music/Scene_1_monster.wav" [loop="true"]
join Idris (Idris_smile) center [animation="Fade In" length="1.0" wait="true"]
if {ChapterTracking.is_evil} == true:
	Idris (Idris_angry): Word travels fast in this town. I hear you've been calling us monsters.
	catherine: What, what are you? I've never seen you in town before.
	Idris (Idris_angry): Of course, you haven't. I am not the kind to mingle with those people.
	Idris (Idris_angry): Even if this body I use used to do that.
	catherine: What do you mean?
	Idris (Idris_angry): Nevermind. We don't like the things you talk about with the villagers here.
	Idris (Idris_angry): And since you are here now, I don't find any reason to keep you alive.
	catherine: No, wait. I didn't mean to...
	- Respond with kindness and understanding
		catherine: I didn't know you heard what I was saying. I don't know you at all.
		Idris (Idris_angry): So you will only put respect on us if you know you are being watched ? Pathethic.
		catherine: No, I'm sorry if it was unfair of me. I don't actually know you at all.
		Idris (Idris_angry): An apology. From a human. Why would I even take that seriously.
		Idris (Idris_angry): Careful around here, the walls have ears and eyes. And we got you in our sight, newcomer.
		leave Idris
		catherine: I geniunely felt threatened this time. But why don't they do nothing to me.
		catherine: I need to be careful next time. I don't think finding that creature that could cure me is even a good idea now.
		[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/BlackBaground.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
		set {EndingTracking.marloch_feeling} += 1.0
	- Respond with fear and condescension
		catherine: Well, can you blame anyone, looking at what you are?
		Idris: Careful. That mouth of yours will get you further trouble than you'd like.
		catherine: You don't scare me.
		Idris: You go around town saying you are looking for one of us, yet you threaten me now.
		Idris: What do you even have in mind.
		Idris: If I were you I would run and quit this town before something happen. No one will save you here.
		catherine: *takes a step back an run*
		catherine: I might have messed up, I need to get myself out of here.
		leave Idris
		[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/BlackBaground.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
		set {EndingTracking.marloch_feeling} -= 1.0
else:
	Idris: I hear you've been rather generous about my character, all things considered.
	catherine: I only said what seemed fair.
	- Dismiss him, stay guarded
		catherine: That doesn't mean I trust you, though.
		Idris: Trust is overrated. I didn't ask for it.
		leave Idris
		[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/BlackBaground.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
		set {EndingTracking.marloch_feeling} -= 1.0
	- Validate him, warm up to him
		catherine: For what it's worth, I meant it. I don't think you're what people say.
		Idris: ...Noted.
		leave Idris
		[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/BlackBaground.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
		set {EndingTracking.marloch_feeling} += 1.0
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/BlackBaground.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
join Marloch (Marloch_angry) left [animation="Fade In" length="1.0" wait="true"]
Marloch (Marloch_angry): You know what I want to know.
join Idris right [animation="Fade In" length="1.0" wait="true"]
Idris: She ain't worth the trouble, she will leave soon.
Marloch (Marloch_angry): It's me who decides if she is worth the trouble or not. Just tell me what she wants.
Idris: She looks sick. And she seems to have knowns something before coming to Shateroo.
Marloch (Marloch_angry): I see...
leave Marloch [animation="Fade Out" length="1.0" wait="true"]
leave Idris [animation="Fade Out" length="1.0" wait="true"]
